## Fixes in the commit

- F681 (lesson-flow.tsx): the end-region focus effect keeps focus({ preventScroll: true }) and
  then, only when getBoundingClientRect().top >= window.innerHeight, calls
  scrollIntoView({ block: "nearest" }) on the region. A region that is already inside the
  viewport moves no scroll, so the round 3 result (scrollY 0 in all 40 runs) holds for days 1
  to 4, and on day 5 at 1920x1080 the page stays still. On day 5 at 1366x768, where the UX
  role measured the region box at 816 to 1388 in a 768 px viewport, the region now scrolls
  into view, so a keyboard user sees where the focus went.
- Tests (phase4-lesson-focus.test.tsx): one case mocks the region box below the viewport
  (top 900 in a 768 px window) and asserts the scrollIntoView call with block "nearest"; one
  case mocks the box inside the viewport (top 200) and asserts no call. The stub removes
  itself from Element.prototype after each case.

